   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The time perspective with «bevor»",
     "texto": [
      "Unlike «nachdem», the conjunction **bevor** (before) introduces an action that is **later** than the one described in the main clause (Nachzeitigkeit).",
      "In everyday or work sentences, both clauses usually have the same tense:",
      "1. In the present for routines and recommendations: **Bevor du nach Hause gehst, schalte bitte das Licht aus**.",
      "2. In the past when narrating: **Bevor er die Firma verließ, hatte er alle Daten gesichert** (before leaving the company, he had saved all the data).",
      "Remember that «bevor» is subordinating: the conjugated verb moves to the last position in the subordinate clause."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Conjunction",
     "columnas": [
